# Single selected routed-permutation and geometry fixture

Declared before execution. Fixed input is the previously saved literal L_b=8,Q_mem=3,n_old=2,M=4 geometry, whose result file has SHA256 b22a3143e5df11e1c15220dbe6f1ac83c1ff623dc2559733cc1c0877e4dbc56f. Read only its coordinate and declared-edge inventories; do not execute its scientific program or reuse its inverse checks as new evidence. The new appended memory roots are the three prescribed upper-right cycle corners and ray lengths43,35,43. No parameter search or fitting follows output.

Enumerate each auxiliary component lexicographically. Use lexicographically ordered breadth-first shortest paths to the selected root. Pair auxiliary j with memory-ray vertex j, concatenate its root path and the initial j ray edges, and generate the chronological2d-1 endpoint-transposition word. Execute the entire serial word on distinct integer register labels. Compare the final permutation to the independently specified product of endpoint swaps, including original-site identity. Verify all paths/steps are NN, no original site is used as transit, intermediate labels are restored by each complete endpoint word, and P_i=m_i²+2sum ell_j. Record the actual complete word, paths and final label permutation.

Geometry checks include freshness and mutual disjointness of all memory sites, root degrees, the saturated a1 neighbor inventory, and every NN adjacency touching A or E. Enumerate declared and omitted edges including same-component, cross-component, old/fresh and new memory interactions. Test the specific proposed two additional omitted memory-to-auxiliary edges and preserve any discrepancy. These checks are predeclared here, not retrospective additions.

One fixed negative mutation: omit the reverse half of the first endpoint word with d>=2 and retain the rest of the route. Its final permutation must differ from the target. Memory consumption is checked by the nominal final label map: each memory site contains its paired original auxiliary record. This is not a numerical quantum-state, phase or dynamics test.

The only scientific execution is one invocation of exact_route_fixture.py through the presealed run_once.py recorder, which writes source-at-launch hashes before the child starts and records complete stdout/stderr, return code and output hashes afterwards. Failure or exception is preserved; no rerun is planned. No full Hilbert matrix, inverse, continuous propagator or arbitrary-H numerical model is formed. The general family and full-output compensated-control theorem remain analytic and require independent review.
